<title>USA: World Bank backs Azerbaijan-Turkey pipeline study.</title>
<headline>World Bank backs Azerbaijan-Turkey pipeline study.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The World Bank agreed on Thursday to lend Turkey $5 million to help finance studies on the feasibility and environmental impact of pipelines to export oil from Azerbaijan.</p>
<p>The proposed export route for Azeri oil is from Baku to Turkey's Mediterranean port of Ceyhan.</p>
<p>The $5.25 million studies would be designed to evaluate the best route for a pipeline to ship up to 45 million tonnes a year of Azeri oil and recommend &quot;a realistic, commercial structure&quot; for building and operating the pipeline, the World Bank said.</p>
<p>The bank said it was not committing to help finance the pipeline itself &quot;because it is expected that the pipeline would be built and financed by the private sector,&quot; led by Turkey's oil and gas pipeline company BOTAS.</p>
</text>
